# Central pinned refs for in-lab player builds (Plan A).
#
# One source of truth so every Nim player compiles against the SAME crewrift game
# version. Sourced by tools/build_player.sh and passed to the Dockerfiles as
# --build-arg. See docs/designs/building_players.md.

# The crewrift game commit the Nim players (notsus, suspectra) compile against, and
# the default for tools/build_expand_replay.sh.
#
# DELIBERATELY PINNED — do NOT point this at `master`, and it can't be auto-resolved.
# It must match the game version the LEAGUE actually runs (the last *deployed* game),
# but the platform exposes no way to map that to a commit: the deployed image is
# `crewrift:latest`, the repo has no release tags, and the manifest's source_urls point
# at `master` generically. And `master` is NOT a safe proxy — it runs ahead of what's
# deployed: building at `master` tip on 2026-06-09 hash-failed on a fresh live replay
# (deployment lag), while d9f6b30 expands current replays cleanly. So this is a
# deliberate pin, bumped rarely (only when the league redeploys the game).
#   How you'll know to bump: build_expand_replay starts `hash-fail`ing on FRESH replays
#   (see docs/crewrift-replays.md §B) — that's the signal the league redeployed; then
#   try a newer commit until a fresh replay expands cleanly, and update this.
# Current value (crewrift d9f6b30 / v0.1.40) matches the live game as of 2026-06-09.
#
# STALENESS WARNING (2026-07-21): the deployed league game is now v0.4.68
# (commit 34a97a3) — this pin is ~3 minor versions behind. The consequence of
# letting it drift silently is real: the game renamed its player palette on
# 2026-06-24 (coworld-crewrift 1cbd4de) and crewborg's PLAYER_COLOR_NAMES stayed
# on the old names for a month — every slot ≥ 1 mis-labelled — before the v107
# audit caught it (fixed in 2a13256; now guarded by
# crewborg/tests/test_palette_crosscheck.py, which diffs PLAYER_COLOR_NAMES
# against sim.nim at the deployed ref in .cache/crewrift-src/).
# This ref is DELIBERATELY NOT BUMPED to 34a97a3: it pins the game source the
# vendored Nim players (notsus, suspectra) compile against, and their sources
# were written against the 0.1.x game API — bumping ~0.3 versions risks breaking
# their builds untested. Bump it only alongside a verified rebuild of both Nim
# players (tools/build_player.sh), or override per-tool: build_expand_replay.sh
# --ref 34a97a3 already builds the league-matched expander without touching this.
CREWRIFT_REF=d9f6b30

# The shared player SDK that crewborg (Python) builds against — installed from the
# coworld-tools monorepo's GitHub source tarball (the players repo moved there as the
# `players/` subdirectory; the Dockerfile installs `…coworld-tools/archive/<ref>.tar.gz
# #subdirectory=players`). `main` is resolved by build_player.sh to coworld-tools' current
# main commit via `git ls-remote`, so the Docker layer cache busts exactly when main moves.
# (A literal `main` build-arg is a cache trap: the pip-install layer caches on the unchanged
# URL string, so a moved main silently keeps the stale SDK.) Set a SHA here to build a
# specific commit.
# NB local `uv run` ALSO installs the SDK from coworld-tools now (2026-06-26): the root
# `pyproject.toml` [tool.uv.sources] pins `players[bedrock]` to the coworld-tools archive
# TARBALL (`…/archive/<sha>.tar.gz#subdirectory=players`), not a git source. A tarball
# excludes submodules, which sidesteps the broken `players/users/relh/co-gas` submodule that
# breaks uv's recursive git clone (coworld-tools issue #13). So local dev and the built image
# now run the SAME SDK (Bedrock routing included). Keep the pyproject tarball SHA in sync with
# this ref when bumping (uv can't auto-track `main` for a tarball — bump the SHA + `uv lock`).
# Pinned to e8921a6 (2026-07-06): first coworld-tools main with the SpriteV1 bridge
# (players.player_sdk.sprite_bridge, PR #20) that heartleaf_lab/cady builds on.
#
# ⚠️ DIVERGED 2026-08-07 — local `uv` and this image ref are NO LONGER the same SDK.
# pyproject.toml was bumped to 4dd923d for paintbot: older revisions clamped Sprite-v1
# input masks to 0x7f and silently dropped Button C (the grenade bit). This ref was left
# at e8921a6 deliberately, because bumping it rebuilds crewborg — a live player — against
# an SDK it has not been tested on. Re-sync only with a crewborg rebuild + retest; see
# the root TODO.md item.
PLAYERS_SDK_REF=e8921a6b18484030d8704277e4c52d3aae5c8917
